React guarantees that the code inside ` useLayoutEffect ` and any state
updates scheduled inside it will be processed **before the browser repaints
the screen.** This lets you render the tooltip, measure it, and re-render the
tooltip again without the user noticing the first extra render. In other
words, ` useLayoutEffect ` blocks the browser from painting.

