####  Exposing a subset of the API with an imperative handle

Show Details

In the above example, ` MyInput ` exposes the original DOM input element. This
lets the parent component call ` focus() ` on it. However, this also lets the
parent component do something else—for example, change its CSS styles. In
uncommon cases, you may want to restrict the exposed functionality. You can do
that with ` useImperativeHandle ` :

App.js

