###  Custom Parsers

In eslintrc files, importing a custom parser is similar to importing a plugin:
you use a string to specify the name of the parser.

In flat config files, import a custom parser as a module, then assign it to
the ` languageOptions.parser ` property of a configuration object.

For example, this eslintrc config file uses the ` @babel/eslint-parser `
parser:



    // .eslintrc.js

    module.exports = {
        // ...other config
        parser: "@babel/eslint-parser",
        // ...other config
    };


